// Survive transient apt mirror failures (HTTP 500 / timeout) in the SHIPPED image
// at runtime - most importantly the first-boot vacti-engine .deb install and any
// later apt use. The build-time fetch is covered separately by lb config
// --apt-options in auto/config (this includes.chroot overlay lands after the heavy
// install-packages step, so it cannot help that fetch; it ships for runtime).
// http.kali.org and deb.debian.org are DNS round-robins across third-party
// mirrors; one mirror returning 500/timeout on a single file should not be fatal.
// A retry re-resolves the round-robin DNS, so it usually lands on a healthy mirror.
// Applies to both the Debian base and the pinned Kali source. Not a credential and
// does not wire any vacti apt source - the thin-bootstrap invariant is preserved.
Acquire::Retries "5";
Acquire::Retries::Delay::Maximum "15";
